Looking at the current best approach, it only estimates position (centroid) while using fixed shape/size/orientation/amplitude for every image. Since the actual ellipses vary a lot in size, orientation, and brightness, this leaves huge residual error. I'll replace the fixed shape params with actual weighted second-moment statistics (to get true semi-axes and orientation) and estimate amplitude from the brightest pixels, keeping the same ellipse-rendering decode but with a size-independent edge ramp.

